Alloy: winemac.drv: keep a hidden cursor hidden.

Games hide the cursor and use the mouse for looking around, but the macOS cursor kept showing up over them:
- macOS shows a hidden cursor again by itself (the menu bar or Dock sliding in, notifications, app switching,
  screenshots) without telling the app. Wine still believed it hidden and never hid it again, so it stayed on screen
  until the game changed its cursor. While the game wants it hidden, hide it again at most every 0.25 s as the mouse
  moves; the hide count stays at one.
- A game that confines the cursor to its window can push it onto the window's right or bottom edge, which
  NSMouseInRect counts as outside the window, and the menu bar, a notification or another app's window can lie over
  a fullscreen game. Wine then showed the cursor and dropped the mouse moves. While the cursor is confined, or a
  fullscreen window that hid it had it, that window stays the target.

